answer.short:
Divide the circle into its four quadrant arcs:

$y=\sqrt{49-x^2},\quad -7\le x\le0$;

$y=\sqrt{49-x^2},\quad 0\le x\le7$;

$y=-\sqrt{49-x^2},\quad -7\le x\le0$;

$y=-\sqrt{49-x^2},\quad 0\le x\le7$.

Each arc passes both the vertical and horizontal line tests, so each represents a function with an inverse.
